---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';

import carSeatImage from '@/assets/car-leather-seat/car-seat.png';
import stitchingImage from '@/assets/car-leather-seat/stitching.jpg';
import HondaOdysseyImage from '@/assets/car-leather-seat/honda-odyssey-seats.jpg';
import hondaSeatsRoseImage from '@/assets/car-leather-seat/honda-seats-rose.png';
import beforeAfterLexusImage from '@/assets/car-leather-seat/before-after-lexus.png';
import beforeAfterMazdaImage from '@/assets/car-leather-seat/before-after-mazda.png';
import beforeAfterHondaImage from '@/assets/car-leather-seat/before-after-honda.png';
import beforeAfterRepairImage from '@/assets/car-leather-seat/before-after-repair.png';
import beforeAfterRepair2Image from '@/assets/car-leather-seat/before-after-repair-2.png';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>Car Leather Seat Rewrap and Repair in Singapore | Five Star Auto Leather</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Trusted car interior leather seat repair and rewrap in Singapore with vegan-only man-made materials, in-house custom production, and 20 years of workmanship."
    />
  </Fragment>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="order-2 sm:order-1">
      <Image
        src={carSeatImage}
        alt="Mercedes CLA180 seats rewrap in Moonlight White leather showcasing refreshed auto interior repair finish"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[800]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="custom-featured h-full w-full bg-black object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="order-1 flex items-center justify-center bg-black px-4 py-8 sm:order-2 sm:px-16">
      <div
        class="title-slide-up flex h-full flex-col items-center justify-center text-center text-white sm:items-start sm:text-left"
      >
        <h1 class="text-4xl">Car Leather Seat Rewrap and Repair Services in Singapore</h1>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Are your car seats cracked, peeling or worn? Five Star specialises in car seat rewrap and
          repair, backed by more than 20 years of hands-on work in Singapore. Our in-house services
          restore comfort and help protect resale value.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/contact-us"
          class="mt-8 inline-block w-36 rounded bg-red-700 px-4 py-2 text-center text-sm font-medium transition-colors hover:bg-red-600"
        >
          Get in Touch
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-7xl flex-col items-center gap-8 px-4 py-8 sm:px-6">
    <div class="text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl">Deciding on a Type of Upholstery Service</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        With so many car seat upholstery options available, it can be difficult to know which
        service is right for your vehicle. The best choice depends on your car's current interior
        condition, your budget, and your future intentions for your car, from choosing a targeted
        repair, doing a partial rewrap, or creating a fully customised interior.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Use the guide below to identify the option that best suits your needs, then visit our
        workshop for a personalised recommendation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <table class="w-full border-collapse border border-gray-300">
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-gray-100">
          <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3 text-left">Your Car's Condition</th>
          <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3 text-left">Type of Upholstery Service</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >Single tear, crack, or worn patch confined to one area of the seat</td
          >
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Targeted leather repair</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >Seat leather is still presentable, but foam has sunken in or lacks comfort on long
            drives</td
          >
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Targeted foam repair</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >One or two seats (e.g. driver's seat) are worn, cracked, peeling or faded, while the
            rest of the cabin remains in good condition</td
          >
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Partial seat rewrap</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >Most seats are worn, cracked, peeling or faded throughout the cabin</td
          >
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Full seats rewrap</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >You want a fresh new look, a colour change, premium materials or a unique interior</td
          >
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Fully customised seats rewrap</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="text-center">
      If you are unsure which car seat repair service you require, contact Five Star Auto Leather
      for a professional assessment. Our team will inspect the condition of your seats in person and
      recommend the most suitable and cost-effective solution.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-6">
      <Image
        src={stitchingImage}
        alt="Close up stitching trim with sewing machine during car seat repair upholstery process"
        loading="lazy"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="h-full w-full object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col justify-center px-4 py-8 lg:col-span-6 lg:px-16">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-center text-2xl lg:text-left">
        Our Auto Interior Rewrap and Repair Process
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-8 text-center lg:text-left">
        Our car dashboard leather rewrap process is handled entirely in-house, from removal and
        preparation to the final quality check. Watch how a full rewrap is done at Five Star Auto
        Leather.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 1: On-Car Assessment</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Bring your car in for a hands-on inspection. We assess the seats in person to identify what
        needs repairing and what needs a full rewrap.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 2: Transparent Quotation</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        A clear quotation with no misleading "from" prices or hidden charges. Just fair pricing
        tailored to your car.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 3: Design Consultation</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Choose your leather colour, grain, stitch style, and finish. Selections are confirmed
        against your actual car under natural light. Too busy to visit? Consultations can also be
        finalised over WhatsApp or call.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 4: In-House Craftsmanship</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Every panel is cut, stitched, and finished inside our workshop by our own team, never
        outsourced.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 5: Final Quality Inspection</h3>
      <p class="mb-8">
        Every seat panel is inspected and test-fitted before final installation, with adjustments
        made on the spot.
      </p>
      <p>
        Watch the <a
          href="https://www.facebook.com/reel/2612823182449712?rdid=KF9iCmvi6fpp6pW9&share_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fshare%2Fr%2F1D8hfZkpBH%2F#"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="font-bold text-gray-600 underline hover:text-gray-900"
          >full car seat rewrap process in action</a
        > or read our{' '}
        <a
          href="/blog/seat-rewrap-process"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="font-bold text-gray-600 underline hover:text-gray-900"
        >
          step-by-step car seat rewrap process guide
        </a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-black">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-7xl flex-col gap-8 px-4 py-8 text-white sm:px-6">
      <div class="text-center">
        <h2 class="text-2xl">How We Do Targeted Car Leather Repair</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Got a perfectly good car seat with just a bit of leather damage, like a hole on the
          driver's bolster or a small tear along the seam? There's no need to replace the whole
          seat. At Five Star, we repair just the damaged spot, so you save on cost and keep the rest
          of the seat intact.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-left text-xl font-bold">Step 1: Cut Out the Damaged Piece</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We mark out the affected area and carefully cut away the damaged patch, keeping the
          surrounding leather untouched.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-left text-xl font-bold">Step 2: Stitch in New Leather</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Our in-house craftsman cuts a matching piece of premium vegan leather and stitches it in,
          blending with the existing seat design and stitch pattern.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-left text-xl font-bold">Step 3: Refit and Inspect</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The repaired panel is refitted onto the seat frame, test-fitted, and inspected before your
          car leaves the workshop.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Watch our <a
            href="https://www.facebook.com/share/r/1D8hfZkpBH/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="font-bold text-gray-400 underline hover:text-gray-100"
            >step-by-step targeted car leather rewrap</a
          > for a closer look at how the patch work is done in our workshop.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-left text-xl font-bold">A Few Repair Tips Worth Knowing</h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0" />
            <span
              >Black seats are the easiest to match. Beiges and browns are the hardest, as shade
              differences show up more under natural light.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0" />
            <span
              >Repair is worth it only for small damage. If wear is spread across the seat, a
              partial or full rewrap gives a cleaner result.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0" />
            <span
              >Spray painting works for surface fading, but it may not last on high-touch areas like
              the driver's bolster.</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Not sure if your car qualifies? Send us a picture of the damaged area for a quick
          preliminary assessment, or drop by our Ang Mo Kio workshop.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="order-1 lg:order-2">
      <Image
        src={HondaOdysseyImage}
        alt="Honda Odyssey pilot seats rewrap in Winter Snow leather showcasing premium car leather repair and rewrap finish"
        loading="lazy"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="custom-featured-2 h-full w-full object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="order-2 flex h-full flex-col justify-center gap-8 px-4 py-8 lg:order-1 lg:px-16">
      <div class="text-center lg:text-left">
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-2xl">Premium Vegan Leather Built for Singapore's Climate</h2>
        <p>
          Every car leather repair and rewrap at our workshop is finished with premium
          automotive-grade vegan microfiber leather. Engineered specifically for cars, it delivers
          the same luxurious look and feel as traditional upholstery while standing up to
          Singapore's heat, humidity, and UV exposure.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl font-bold">Why It Works Well for Singapore Cabins</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-red-600" />
            <span>Soft and luxurious to the touch, on par with high-end car interiors</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-red-600" />
            <span>UV resistant, holds its finish under long hours in the sun</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-red-600" />
            <span>Colour stable, keeps the cabin looking newer for longer</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-red-600" />
            <span>Scratch resistant and wipes down cleanly, no conditioners required</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-red-600" />
            <span>Easy to maintain year-round in Singapore's humid climate</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl font-bold">Engineered for Automotive Use</h3>
        <p>
          Automotive-grade microfiber leather sits in a category of its own. Unlike the synthetic
          materials you might find in furniture or fashion accessories, this leather is engineered
          specifically for the automotive industry to withstand years of daily use. Soft, luxurious,
          and built to hold up to real driving conditions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl font-bold">Our Exclusive Vegan Leather Commitment</h3>
        <p class="mb-2">
          After more than 20 years in the industry, taking over the family business came with one
          clear decision. Go exclusively vegan. Not because it costs less. Not because it's trendy.
          We believe automotive-grade microfiber leather is the right material for modern car
          interiors, and it's what we'd choose for our own cars.
        </p>
        <p>
          Watch our founders share the story behind the switch in <a
            href="https://www.facebook.com/share/r/1DS7ForvzK/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="font-bold text-gray-600 underline hover:text-gray-900"
            >our vegan leather journey</a
          >, or find out <a
            href="https://www.fivestarautoleather.com/blog/why-choose-vegan-leather"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="font-bold text-gray-600 underline hover:text-gray-900"
            >why we choose vegan leather</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <Image
      src={hondaSeatsRoseImage}
      alt="Honda Nvan seats rewrap in Burgundy Rose leather showcasing bold car interior repair and rewrap transformation"
      loading="lazy"
      widths={[640, 1280]}
      sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
      class="custom-featured h-full w-full object-cover"
    />

    <div class="flex h-full flex-col justify-center px-4 py-8 lg:px-16">
      <h2 class="mb-8 text-center text-2xl">Why Choose Five Star Auto Leather</h2>

      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Transparent Pricing</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Every car seat repair and rewrap is individually quoted based on your vehicle, seat
        condition, and chosen material. No misleading "from" prices, no hidden charges.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Minimal Downtime, Maximum Convenience</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Your car is part of your daily routine. Every part of our car interior repair workflow is
        designed to be smooth, practical, and hassle-free without compromising on quality. Where
        possible, we complete multiple components together to keep your car off the road for as
        little time as possible.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Built for Singapore's Climate</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Premium vegan microfiber leather paired with high-performance, heat-resistant adhesives,
        chosen specifically for Singapore's heat and humidity.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">100% In-House Craftsmanship</h3>
      <p>
        Every car leather repair job is carried out fully in Singapore by our own team. For seat
        rewraps, sewing is done at our own production facility in Batam, with installation completed
        in our Singapore workshop. Full quality control from start to finish, backed by our
        workmanship warranty.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-7xl flex-col items-center gap-8 px-4 py-8 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl">Before & After</h2>

    <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-3">
      <div class="grid w-full gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <Image
          src={beforeAfterLexusImage}
          alt="Before and after Lexus RX300 seats rewrap in Burgundy Rose showcasing full car seat repair result"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          widths={[640, 1280]}
          sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
          class="h-full w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
        />
        <Image
          src={beforeAfterMazdaImage}
          alt="Before and after Mazda MX5 seats rewrap in Coffee Cream highlighting auto interior repair finish"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          widths={[640, 1280]}
          sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
          class="h-full w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
        />
        <Image
          src={beforeAfterHondaImage}
          alt="Before and After of Honda CRZ seats rewrap in Orange"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          widths={[640, 1280]}
          sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
          class="h-full w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="grid w-full gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <Image
          src={beforeAfterRepairImage}
          alt="Before and after targeted car leather repair on driver seat bolster restoring worn patch to clean finish"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          widths={[640, 1280]}
          sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
          class="block h-auto w-full rounded-lg"
        />
        <Image
          src={beforeAfterRepair2Image}
          alt="Before and after targeted car leather repair on driver seat bolster restoring worn patch to clean finish"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          widths={[640, 1280]}
          sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
          class="block h-auto w-full rounded-lg"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-black">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-7xl flex-col gap-8 px-4 py-8 text-white sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="text-center text-2xl">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Can you rewrap any car seats and all interior parts?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Absolutely, we can rewrap any car seat. As for other interior parts, it depends. Some
          components, like plastic handles or casings, aren't meant to be wrapped and we don't
          believe in forcing what doesn't fit. Our rule of thumb? If it came wrapped in leather or
          PVC, we can rewrap it and make it look factory-fitted or better.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">What are the downtimes for the different upholstery services?</h3>
        <table class="mt-4 w-full border-collapse border border-gray-900">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-gray-900">
              <th class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3 text-left">Service Type</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3 text-left">Production Lead Time</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3 text-left">Installation Downtime</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3">Targeted leather repair</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3">Not required</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3">2 to 3 hours per seat</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3">Targeted foam repair</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3">Not applicable</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3">2 to 3 hours per seat</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3">Partial seats rewrap</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3"
                >3 to 4 working days for ordered covers to arrive</td
              >
              <td class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3">2 to 3 hours per seat</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3">Full seats rewrap</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3"
                >3 to 4 working days for ordered covers to arrive</td
              >
              <td class="border border-gray-700 px-4 py-3">Within 1 day</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm">
          <strong>Note:</strong> The above downtimes apply to cars with existing templates. For less
          common car models, we open templates by removing your existing seat covers and sending them
          to our production facility in Batam. This takes around 1 to 1.5 weeks. To minimise your downtime,
          we can fix back the "naked" car seats so your car remains fully drivable while you wait.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">What material options do you offer?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We specialise exclusively in automotive-grade vegan microfiber leather, a next-generation
          material that delivers the same premium look and feel as cowhide, minus the cruelty,
          maintenance hassles, and environmental footprint.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Crafted from ultra-fine fibres that replicate the structure of natural leather, it feels
          soft and supple to the touch. Engineered for modern car interiors, our microfiber leather
          is UV-resistant, scratch-resistant, and easy to clean. Our collection comes in two
          finishes:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-5">
          <li>
            <strong>Standard Full Grain</strong> for a more textured, natural feel
          </li>
          <li>
            <span><strong>Premium Smooth Grain</strong> for a sleek, soft, and luxe finish</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          To complement your interior, we also carry other premium vegan materials such as Alcantara
          for seats and velvet fabric for roof linings. For commercial or rental vehicles, we offer
          a durable and cost-effective PVC option that's thicker than standard market versions,
          measuring 1.1mm for enhanced strength.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Want to dive deeper? Check out our blog post{' '}
          <a
            href="https://www.fivestarautoleather.com/blog/types-of-car-leather"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="font-bold text-gray-400 underline hover:text-gray-100"
          >
            “3 Types of Car Leather and How to Identify Them”
          </a>{' '}
          for a more in-depth read.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">What design elements can I customise for my car?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">You can personalise your interior with:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-5">
          <li>
            Material type (such as textured vs. smooth grain, fabric alternatives like Alcantara)
          </li>
          <li>Colour combinations</li>
          <li>Leather trim details such as piping</li>
          <li>Stitching colour & pattern</li>
          <li>Embroidered logo or branding</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Google is your best friend for design inspiration, but do remember to keep your seat's
          original contours in mind as they can't be changed. The smartest designs work with your
          car's curves, not against them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">
          How durable is your leather? Is it scratch resistant and pet friendly?
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Our leathers are automotive-grade, UV-resistant, and wear-tested for long-lasting
          performance even under Singapore's climate. It is scratch resistant and pet friendly,
          especially when it comes to wet messes. We do, however, recommend using a pet mat on top
          of the seats for even easier upkeep and to extend your leather's lifespan.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          See how tough our leather really is in our{' '}
